.TH "ODIR-DOT-AUTHORIZED" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-dot\-authorized \- \&.authorized: Check for authorization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&.authorized [job=<job>] [client=<client>] [storage=<storage>] [schedule=<schedule>] [pool=<pool>] [cmd=<cmd>] [fileset=<fileset>] [catalog=<catalog>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Checks whether the own console may access a resource or command and answers authorized or not authorized. The check uses the ACLs of the Console resource and its profiles (Job, Client, Storage, Schedule, Pool, Command, FileSet and Catalog ACL). User interfaces such as bareos\-webui use it to show buttons only when permitted. It only reads.
.PP
Keys are case\-insensitive, and only the ACL is checked, not whether the resource exists. With several arguments the last known one decides. Without arguments, with unknown keys only or with a key lacking a value the answer is not authorized, even for an unrestricted console.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "\&.authorized"
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "schedule=<schedule>"
Schedule name (name; values from .schedule)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.TP
.B "cmd=<cmd>"
Command name (name; a command name)
.TP
.B "fileset=<fileset>"
FileSet name (name; values from .filesets)
.TP
.B "catalog=<catalog>"
Catalog name (name; values from .catalogs)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "\&.authorized cmd=purge"
check whether the console may run purge
.TP
.B "\&.authorized client=bareos\-fd"
check access to client bareos\-fd
